James inquired about adding a column to an HTML table that featured a filled circle, with colors specified by hex codes. I provided a solution that involved creating a new column utilizing a `<span>` element styled as a circle with CSS. I included a code example demonstrating the implementation, specifying the use of the `color-circle` class to achieve a circular shape and apply color through the `background-color` property. The code also allowed for dynamic color changes by modifying the hex codes. I encouraged James to reach out for further assistance if needed.
